WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:02.602
-Guys,
it is the end of the week.

00:00:02.602 --> 00:00:03.936
And that's usually when I catch
up with some personal stuff.

00:00:03.936 --> 00:00:05.471
You know, I check my in-box
or return some e-mails,

00:00:05.471 --> 00:00:07.474
and, of course, send out
"thank you" notes.

00:00:07.474 --> 00:00:08.541
-Whoo!

00:00:08.541 --> 00:00:09.675
-Well, I was running
a bit behind,

00:00:09.675 --> 00:00:11.144
so I thought,
if you guys wouldn't mind,

00:00:11.144 --> 00:00:12.812
I'd like to write out my weekly
"thank you" notes right now.

00:00:12.812 --> 00:00:13.979
Is that...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:13.979 --> 00:00:15.748
James -- James, can I get

00:00:15.748 --> 00:00:17.417
some "thank you note" writing
music, please?

00:00:17.417 --> 00:00:21.020
♪♪

00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:22.321
-[ Chuckles ]

00:00:22.321 --> 00:00:24.156
♪♪

00:00:24.156 --> 00:00:25.925
-Alright.
You moved a little bit.

00:00:25.925 --> 00:00:28.961
[ Laughter ]
A little bit of movement there.

00:00:28.961 --> 00:00:30.429
♪♪

00:00:30.429 --> 00:00:33.433
Thank you, candy corn,
for looking like

00:00:33.433 --> 00:00:35.468
a 5-year-old's finger painting
of Donald Trump.

00:00:35.468 --> 00:00:37.537
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:40.473 --> 00:00:42.108
♪♪

00:00:42.108 --> 00:00:45.278
Thank you, apple picking,
for giving couples

00:00:45.278 --> 00:00:47.447
who are tired
of getting into fights at Ikea

00:00:47.447 --> 00:00:48.681
an outdoor alternative.

00:00:48.681 --> 00:00:52.251
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:52.251 --> 00:00:53.987
I'm going to put them
in the envelope later.

00:00:53.987 --> 00:00:56.723
[ Laughter ]

00:00:56.723 --> 00:01:00.093
-I mean, wow, you're really
just phoning it in today, huh?

00:01:00.093 --> 00:01:01.460
[ Laughter ]

00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:03.529
There's no gloss.

00:01:03.529 --> 00:01:05.965
-No, it's not --
no, there is no --

00:01:05.965 --> 00:01:08.634
there's never going to be gloss.
-Okay.

00:01:08.634 --> 00:01:10.303
So how come you're not putting
them in the envelope now?

00:01:10.303 --> 00:01:11.704
Because it's the Apocalypse?

00:01:11.704 --> 00:01:14.274
-No. I'm not doing it
because I figured --

00:01:14.274 --> 00:01:16.175
well, it just takes
a little extra beat of time.

00:01:16.175 --> 00:01:18.244
I'll -- I'll -- I'll lick
the envelopes on the next two.

00:01:18.244 --> 00:01:20.880
-Dude, after like 17 years

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:22.781
of, like, you know,
"Thank You Notes"

00:01:22.781 --> 00:01:24.484
where you put it
in the envelope,

00:01:24.484 --> 00:01:26.552
now, okay, we don't even --

00:01:26.552 --> 00:01:28.021
we can't even look forward
to that on a Friday.

00:01:28.021 --> 00:01:29.055
Great.

00:01:29.055 --> 00:01:31.958
[ Laughter ]

00:01:31.958 --> 00:01:34.561
-Tariq, not everything
can be as glossy as your shoes.

00:01:34.561 --> 00:01:35.828
[ Laughter ]

00:01:35.828 --> 00:01:37.429
-Yo!

00:01:37.429 --> 00:01:38.431
That's it.

00:01:38.431 --> 00:01:39.499
♪♪

00:01:39.499 --> 00:01:41.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:43.703
♪♪

00:01:43.703 --> 00:01:45.438
[ Laughter ]

00:01:45.438 --> 00:01:48.141
I saw you searching
and searching and searching.

00:01:48.141 --> 00:01:50.275
[ Laughter ]

00:01:50.275 --> 00:01:53.178
[ Laughter continues ]

00:01:53.178 --> 00:01:55.147
You got me. You got me.
Okay.

00:01:55.147 --> 00:01:57.216
-Alright. Alright.
Here we go.

00:01:57.216 --> 00:01:58.417
♪♪

00:01:58.417 --> 00:01:59.618
Alright, come on, James.

00:01:59.618 --> 00:02:00.953
Alright, here we go.

00:02:00.953 --> 00:02:02.555
♪♪

00:02:02.555 --> 00:02:06.526
Thank you, Dunkin's
new Spicy Ghost Pepper Donut

00:02:06.526 --> 00:02:08.228
for explaining their new slogan,

00:02:08.228 --> 00:02:10.029
"American gets runs on Dunkin'."

00:02:10.029 --> 00:02:11.797
[ Laughter ]

00:02:11.797 --> 00:02:14.367
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:15.501
I did it for you.

00:02:15.501 --> 00:02:17.203
That's for you.

00:02:17.203 --> 00:02:20.273
[ Chuckles ]

00:02:20.273 --> 00:02:21.507
♪♪

00:02:21.507 --> 00:02:24.243
Thank you, pumpkin carving,
for teaching kids

00:02:24.243 --> 00:02:27.280
that Halloween isn't just about
taking candy from strangers --

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:29.082
it's also about
playing with knives.

00:02:29.082 --> 00:02:31.684
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:36.522 --> 00:02:37.923
♪♪

00:02:37.923 --> 00:02:41.827
Thank you, leaves turning red,
or as trees put it,

00:02:41.827 --> 00:02:44.597
"OMG, this is so embarrassing."

00:02:44.597 --> 00:02:46.299
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.299 --> 00:02:47.600
-Oho!

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:50.269
[ Laughter ]

00:02:50.269 --> 00:02:52.004
[ Chuckles ]

00:02:52.004 --> 00:02:54.607
Ah. America gets runs.

00:02:54.607 --> 00:02:56.676
[ Laughter ]

00:02:56.676 --> 00:02:57.743
[ Chuckles ]

00:02:57.743 --> 00:02:58.877
♪♪

00:02:58.877 --> 00:03:01.547
Thank you,
removing the A.C. window unit

00:03:01.547 --> 00:03:04.216
at the end of summer,
for being the only chore

00:03:04.216 --> 00:03:06.052
that leads to a possible
manslaughter charge

00:03:06.052 --> 00:03:07.353
if I do it wrong.

00:03:07.353 --> 00:03:09.488
[ Laughter ]

00:03:09.488 --> 00:03:11.791
[ Laughter continues ]

00:03:14.927 --> 00:03:16.763
"Pack everything up.
We're moving."

00:03:16.763 --> 00:03:18.264
[ Laughter ]

00:03:18.264 --> 00:03:20.500
[ Chuckles ]

00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:22.668
♪♪

00:03:22.668 --> 00:03:25.972
Thank you, hot stone massages,

00:03:25.972 --> 00:03:28.274
for the calming sensation
of being branded.

00:03:28.274 --> 00:03:29.976
[ Laughter and applause ]
There you have it.

00:03:29.976 --> 00:03:31.244
Those are my "Thank You Notes,"
everybody.

